Sam starts with \(2\) gallons.  
For each mile the amount of milk left in the bucket is multiplied by \(\frac{2}{3}\).

\[
\begin{aligned}
\text{After 1 mile:}&\quad 2\cdot \frac{2}{3}= \frac{4}{3}\text{ gallons} \\[4pt]
\text{After 2 miles:}&\quad \frac{4}{3}\cdot \frac{2}{3}= \frac{8}{9}\text{ gallons} \\[4pt]
\text{After 3 miles:}&\quad \frac{8}{9}\cdot \frac{2}{3}= \frac{16}{27}\text{ gallons}
\end{aligned}
\]

Thus, when Sam reaches his house the bucket contains  

\[
\boxed{\dfrac{16}{27}}
\] gallons of milk.

